Package: BJMconformal
Title: Conformal Prediction Intervals for Backward Joint Model Predictions
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Wenhao", "Li", email = "wenhaoli.jlu@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Wraps the public prediction functions of the 'BJM' package
    (predictLongitudinal() and predictRisk()) with split conformal
    calibration, giving prediction intervals for future biomarker values,
    lower prediction bounds for the residual event time, and Venn-Abers
    interval-valued risks. Coverage holds over patients whether or not the
    joint model is correctly specified (exactly for biomarkers and for the
    conservative event-time bound; approximately, through inverse
    probability of censoring weights, for the weighted variants).
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: BJM (>= 0.3.0), survival, nlme, stats, utils
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Remotes: wenhaoli18/BJM
Config/testthat/edition: 3
